@page "/AMS"
@rendermode InteractiveServer
@inject NavigationManager navigationManager

<div class="container" >
    <div class="py-4 py-md-5" id="top"></div>
    @* Page header *@
    <header class="mb-4 pb-3" >
        <h1 class="display-6 fw-bold">
            AMS - Application Monitoring System
        </h1>
        <p>
            This was a work project. My manager suggested I implement a system which would automatically run
            some of
            the daily checks which then had to be specifically run every morning by a member of the team.
        </p>
        <p>This was the design I came up with and implemented.</p>
    </header>

    @* The Idea *@
    <section class="card shadow-sm mb-4">
        <div class="card-body p-4">
            <h2 class="card-title">
                The Idea
            </h2>

            <p>
                To implement a website showing the status of various checks that could be added to a database.
                This website could be displayed on a large screen and would update automatically showing changes in
                the status of these checks during the day.
                A summary email was added later which displays the current status of all checks at the time the
                e-mail is sent out.
            </p>

            <p>There are five different check types </p>

            <ul class="list-group">
                <li class="list-group-item">
                    <span class="fw-bold">Cube Checks</span> - Connects to an SSAS
                    server and retrieves the status of each cube defined.
                </li>
                <li class="list-group-item">
                    <span class="fw-bold">Log Checks</span> - Retrieves the log type
                    checks from the database and searches the log supplied for a
                    success or failure word or phrase - only when log changes.
                </li>
                <li class="list-group-item">
                    <span class="fw-bold">SQL Checks</span> - Retrieves the sql type
                    checks from the database and runs the stored procedure
                    specified.
                </li>
                <li class="list-group-item" >
                    <span class="fw-bold">Services Checks</span> - Retrieves the
                    services type checks from the database and checks if the log
                    supplied has been updated within a certain time period e.g. 15 mins.
                </li>
                <li class="list-group-item">
                    <span class="fw-bold">Directory Checks</span> - Retrieves the
                    directory type checks from the database and checks that the
                    directory supplied is empty at a certain time.
                </li>
            </ul>
            <p class="mt-3">
                The webpage displays check types with no issues on the right-side of the screen in green and
                displayed all the checks which failed on the left-hand side in either red (for failed) or yellow (in
                progress).
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

    @* The Implementation *@
    <section class="card shadow-sm mt-3">
        <div class="card-body p-4">
            <h2 class="card-title">
                The Implementation
            </h2>

            <p>
                This was entirely written in C# writing to a SQL Server database using VS2015, SQL Server 2014 and Team 
                Foundation Server 2015. It is currently Live and in use.
            </p>

            <p>There was a lot involved in this project but the main components were as follows: </p>

            <ul class="list-group">
                <li class="list-group-item">
                    <span class="fw-bold">Monitor</span> - A webpage which updates every 5 mins
                    using AJAX showing the status of a set of checks.
                </li>
                <li class="list-group-item">
                    <span class="fw-bold">Database</span> - A database which holds details of
                    each check required so these are soft coded but have a specific
                    check type. It also holds the results of checks run in a log table and tracks progress of each
                    check in an activity table.
                </li>
                <li class="list-group-item">
                    <span class="fw-bold">Performance Counters</span> 
                    - It updates Performance Counters on the server which can be read by <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/System_Center_Operations_Manager">SCOM</a>. 
                    The counters are set to 0 if the check passes and 1 if they fail.
                </li>
                <li class="list-group-item">
                    <span class="fw-bold">Full CRUD functionality</span> - A maintenance page where the codes
                    and checks can be maintained.
                </li>
                <li class="list-group-item">
                    <span class="fw-bold">Email</span> - It sends out a daily checks email to
                    a distribution list held on the database with a snapshot view
                    as at that time - currently 8:00AM. It holds the status of all checks in one email.
                </li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </section>

    @* Footer *@
    <footer class="mt-4 pt-4 pb-3">
        <div class="row mb-3">
            <div class="col-6">
                <button class="btn btn-primary" @onclick="() => ReturnButton()">Return to home</button>
            </div>
            <div class="col-6 mt-1">
                <a href="ams#top" class="link-secondary">
                    Back to top ↑
                </a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </footer>

</div>


@code {
    private void ReturnButton() => navigationManager!.NavigateTo("/");
}
